            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Persian for a hairdresser's, then the Persian for a watchmaker."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: شهربازی",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "شهربازی (shahrbâzi) — \"an amusement park, a funfair\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "بچه ها روز جمعه به شهربازی رفتند. Bachche-hâ ruz-e jom'e be shahrbâzi raftand. The children went to the funfair on Friday."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Literally 'play-town'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "shahrbâzi is a native compound of shahr 'town', from Middle Persian šahr (EtymDB), and bâzi 'play', usually traced to Middle Persian wāzīg."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
