          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "پارک جنگلی (pârk-e jangali) — \"a forest park, a wooded park\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "جمعه ها مردم در پارک جنگلی کباب درست میکنند. Jom'e-hâ mardom dar pârk-e jangali kabâb dorost mikonand. On Fridays people make kebabs in the forest park."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Many Iranian towns have a pârk-e jangali on their edge for picnics."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "pârk-e jangali is built from pârk, a loan usually traced to French parc, and jangali 'wooded', from jangal 'forest', usually traced to Sanskrit jaṅgala."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
