          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ta'til shodan is built from ta'til 'closure, a holiday', borrowed from Arabic taʿṭīl 'suspension, a break' (EtymDB), and the native verb shodan 'to become'."
            }
          ]
